      "title": "Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib",
      "intro": "Known for: Uncle of the Prophet ﷺ, about three years older; kept Zamzam; forefather of the Abbasid caliphs.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Uncle of the Prophet ﷺ, about three years older; kept Zamzam; forefather of the Abbasid caliphs. Full name: al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Hashim. Father: Abdul Muttalib. Born in Makkah. Passed away in 32 AH / February 653 CE at Madinah.\nA half-brother of the Prophet's ﷺ father Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib (his mother was Natila bint Janab). He was a wealthy merchant who took over Zamzam and the watering of the pilgrims after his father. He protected the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah and spoke at the Second Pledge of al-Aqaba, but he fought with the polytheists at Badr, where he was captured and ransomed. He openly joined the Muslims by the Conquest of Makkah, stood by the Prophet ﷺ at Hunayn, and died in Madinah in Uthman's caliphate. His wife Umm al-Fadl (Lubaba bint al-Harith) was among the first women to accept Islam. The Abbasid caliphs descend from their son ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās.",
      "keyTakeaway": "Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib: Uncle of the Prophet ﷺ, about three years older; kept Zamzam; forefather of the Abbasid caliphs.",
