      "title": "Al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī",
      "intro": "Known for: Grandson of the Prophet ﷺ; made peace with Mu'awiya (41 AH).",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Grandson of the Prophet ﷺ; made peace with Mu'awiya (41 AH). Full name: Al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Hashim. Father: Ali ibn Abi Talib. Born in Madinah. Passed away in Safar 49–50 AH / 670 CE at Madinah.\nAl-Hasan ibn Ali.pdf\nGrandson of the Prophet ﷺ — Leader of Youth of Jannah\n- Born: 625 CE (3 AH)\n- Died: 670 CE (50 AH)\n- Age: 45\n- Cause of death: Poisoned (Sunni view: by political enemies — possibly by his wife Ja'dah bint al-Ash'ath; Allah knows best)\n- Burial: Jannat al-Baqī', Madinah\n- The Prophet ﷺ loved him deeply\n- Called Sayyid (\"leader\") by the Prophet\n- United the Ummah by handing the caliphate to Mu'āwiyah (RA) — ending civil war\n- Known for generosity, mercy, and intelligence\n- Sometimes unity is more important than winning\n- Patience in politics and leadership\n- Choosing peace to protect the Ummah\n---\n1. The little boy trys to get the prophet those and falls on his face and cries and the prophet comforts him and seeks forgiveness from the congregation cause he can't bare the upsetness of\n2. He says this son of mine is a leader he is destined for greatness\n3. The prophet called him his son.\n1. The prophet lost all his boys\n4. When Hasan was born the prophet walked into ali House and said where is my boy like a loving grandfather. He asked what his name was and Ali named him War I'm Arabic. Cause he liked hard names. The prophet changed his name to Hasan for eccellent. Ali did the same thing to husayn and the prophet did the same thing and their 3rd kid who died. Funny that Ali tried to name them War\n1. Btw nobody was named these names before something similar like husayn like cheif rabi Abdullah Ibn musalah\n2.",
      "keyTakeaway": "Al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī: Grandson of the Prophet ﷺ; made peace with Mu'awiya (41 AH).",
