      "title": "Ali ibn Abi Talib",
      "intro": "Known for: Fourth caliph; cousin and son-in-law of the Prophet ﷺ; first child to accept Islam.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Fourth caliph; cousin and son-in-law of the Prophet ﷺ; first child to accept Islam. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Hashim. Father: Abu Talib. Born in Makkah. Passed away in 21 Ramadan 40 AH / January 661 CE at Kufa.\n[!star] ⭐ Famous For\n- Cousin of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ\n- Husband of Fatimah al-Zahra\n- Father of Hasan ibn Ali and Husayn ibn Ali\n- Fourth Rightly Guided Caliph\n- One of the Ten Promised Paradise\n- Among the earliest Muslims; commonly described as the first boy/child to accept Islam\n- Famous for his courage, knowledge, and closeness to the Prophet ﷺ\n- Given the banner by the Prophet ﷺ during Battle of Khaybar\n---\n- Father: Abu Talib ibn Abd al-Muttalib\n- Mother: Fatimah bint Asad\n- Cousin: Prophet Muhammad ﷺ\nFatimah al-Zahra\nDaughter of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.\nChildren:\nUmm al-Banin\nChildren:\nLayla bint Masud\nChildren:\nAsma bint Umays\nChildren:\nUmamah bint Abi al-As\nUmamah was the granddaughter of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ through his daughter Zaynab bint Muhammad.\nChild:\nUmm Said bint Urwah\nChild:\n---\nKhawlah bint Ja'far al-Hanafiyyah\nMother of:\nAl-Sahba bint Rabiah\n---\nHe is commonly described as the first boy or child to accept Islam and was among the earliest Muslims.\n---\nThe Prophet ﷺ announced that he would give the banner to a man who loved Allah and His Messenger and whom Allah and His Messenger loved.\nHis caliphate included major internal conflicts such as:\n---\n- The Prophet's ﷺ cousin\n- Raised closely around the Prophet ﷺ\n- One of his earliest followers\n- His son-in-law through Fatimah al-Zahra\n- Father of his grandsons Hasan ibn Ali and Husayn ibn Ali\n---\n- Year: 40 AH / 661 CE\n- Death_Place: Kufa\n- Killed by: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muljam\n- Cause: Mortally wounded in an assassination attack\nSee: The death of Ali\n---\nHe had a few concubines, common among Arab nobles of that era.\n- Mother of Muhammad al-Asghar\n- Mother of Ruqayyah\n- Died: 680 CE (Karbala)\n- Accolades: Banner-bearer of Husayn; symbol of loyalty and bravery\n- ‘Awn and Yahya (from Asmā’)",
      "keyTakeaway": "Ali ibn Abi Talib: Fourth caliph; cousin and son-in-law of the Prophet ﷺ; first child to accept Islam.",
