      "explanationContent": "Known for: Served the Prophet ﷺ for ten years; one of the last Companions to die. Full name: Anas ibn Malik ibn al-Nadr al-Ansari. Tribe: Khazraj, clan of Banu Najjar. Father: Malik ibn al-Nadr. Born in Madinah. Passed away in 93 AH / 712 CE at Basra.\nlongest living sahabi\n1. His mom wanted Dua for him and went to the prophet to make Dua for her son\n2. They used to say if Anas flipped over a rock there would be gold because of his luck\n1. People would want to sign so many business deals with him and not just to do business just to have him sign it so that there would be baraka in the business because he was rich\n3. Anas also had a very large family where he couldn't even count how many grandkids he had\n4. He said the prophet never had a problem with him and not even a ooof",
