      "title": "Julaybib",
      "intro": "Known for: Companion of unknown lineage, married at the Prophet's ﷺ request; martyred after killing seven.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Companion of unknown lineage, married at the Prophet's ﷺ request; martyred after killing seven.\n- Known for: The Sahabi with no tribe\n- Tribe: Unknown\n- He is considered from the Ansari\n- We don't know which tribe\n- we don't kno whis full name\n- He was bullied for his height\n- So basically nobody claimed this young man.\n- He was a sweetheart\nJulaybib means he was either wrapped up all the time. Or it refers to his black skin color. Or it refers to his warm embracement.\nWe know for a fact it's not a negative name even if it's a nickname we know this because thr prophet didn't change it.\nWhen the 00 - Main/Islam/Islamic Figures/People/Muhammad ﷺ would always bring Julabib to the front of every gatheirng because people love dealing with him.\nJulaybib would spend more time with the women in medina and play with them meaning he would talk because the men would bully him and this was the early of islam.\nSomeone got jealous that Julaybib was always amongs the women and this was befoer the ayah of hijab.\nThe time the Prophet married someone to Julaybib\nJulaybib dieing in Battle of Badr 5️⃣\nThe prophet does a headcount from the sub tribes and everyone says they're not missing anyone. Then other groups say they're missing this person this person etc. Then the prophet says he's missing one person he's missing julaybib and said let's look fo rhim.\nThey found him laying on the battlefield with 7 men around him. Back then 7 men is very very Impressive.\nThe prophet says he is a part of me and i'm part of him he is from my tribe.\nThe prophet scooped his small body in his arm and then dug his grave. The Prophet did not do his ghusul and burried him with his own two hands.",
      "keyTakeaway": "Julaybib: Companion of unknown lineage, married at the Prophet's ﷺ request; martyred after killing seven.",
      "lessonType": "story",
      "difficulty": 1,
      "xpReward": 10,
