      "title": "ʿUmayr ibn Wahb al-Jumaḥī",
      "intro": "Known for: Came to Madinah after Badr to kill the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam instead.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Came to Madinah after Badr to kill the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam instead. Full name: Umayr ibn Wahb al-Jumahi. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Jumah.\nthe Battle of Badr, Quraysh sent ʿUmayr out as a scout/reconnaissance man to investigate the Muslim army. He rode around their position and estimated that they numbered around 300–310 men. He also checked whether they had hidden reinforcements or an ambush waiting nearby and reported that they did not.\nIslam Web +1\nInterestingly, ʿUmayr later became Muslim. After Badr, he and Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah secretly discussed a plan in Makkah for ʿUmayr to go to Madinah and kill the Prophet ﷺ. When he arrived, ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb recognized him and was immediately suspicious. The Prophet ﷺ told ʿUmayr about the secret conversation he had had with Ṣafwān, after which ʿUmayr accepted Islam.",
      "keyTakeaway": "ʿUmayr ibn Wahb al-Jumaḥī: Came to Madinah after Badr to kill the Prophet ﷺ and accepted Islam instead.",
