      "title": "Aisha bint Abu Bakr",
      "intro": "Known for: Wife of the Prophet ﷺ; leading scholar and narrator of hadith.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Wife of the Prophet ﷺ; leading scholar and narrator of hadith. Full name: Aisha bint Abi Bakr. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Taym. Father: Abū Bakr aṣ-Ṣiddīq. Born in Makkah. Passed away in 57 or 58 AH / c. July 678 CE at Madinah.\nThird Wife — Scholar of Islam\n- Born: 613 CE\n- Died: 678 CE\n- Age: 65\n- Cause: Illness\n- Father: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq (RA)\n- Mother: Umm Rūmān (RA)\n- Greatest female scholar of the Ummah\n- Narrated 2,210 hadiths\n- Experts in fiqh, medicine, poetry\n- People traveled from all lands to learn from her\n- One of the four greatest women in knowledge\n- Strengthening ties with Abu Bakr\n- She would transmit a huge portion of Sunnah\n- Women can be giants of Islamic knowledge\n- Youth + intelligence = blessing for the Ummah\n1. The propeht said she is the most loved\n2. The prophet had traveled with her the most and when the women drew lots he hoped it was her.\n3. she narrated with most hadiths and the second would be Abu Hurayra\n4. Aisha brought so much life to the prophet.\n5. It's like the love from Abu Bakr transfered to her because every time she got mad it's over jealousy over th etoher wives.\n6. The women who perefected their iman\n1. Khadijah\n2. fatima (Queen of the women of jannah)\n3. asia\n4. Maryam\n7. Asiaha was the best part of th meal of the dinner.\n8. Nicknames\n1. A ish\n2. oaish = little\n3. humaira = aisha was descibed as a beaiful women with a redish complesion when shes shy or mad.\n4. Umm abdilah = they were named after your son but she didn't have a child but named her after her nephew and this shows that your paternal aunt is like your mother.\n9. She loved camels like her father and picked up a lot her trats\n1. She loved poetry and studied anscenstry\n2. sharp\n3. atriculate\n4. honest\n10. she was basiclly born muslim because the propeht visted theri home twice a day.\n1. she grew up watching Abu Bakr being beaten up and going unconcious protecting the prophet\n2. she would see that her father would grab his wealth and help the muslims\n3. she would see that her mother and father would perfect the memoriztion of the Quran\n1. She descrtibed her father as someone who cannot control his eyes while reading the Quran.\n11. The Difficult of the porphet life was starting the memroy of the aisha.",
