      "title": "Aminah bint Wahb",
      "intro": "Known for: Mother of the Prophet ﷺ; died at al-Abwa' when he was six.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Mother of the Prophet ﷺ; died at al-Abwa' when he was six. Full name: Aminah bint Wahb ibn Abd Manaf al-Zuhriyya. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Zuhra. Father: Wahb ibn Abd Manaf. Born in Makkah. Passed away in c. 577 CE at al-Abwa'.\nOf Banu Zuhra, the clan of Zuhra ibn Kilab, brother of the Prophet's ﷺ forefather Qusayy. Her husband Abdullah died before their son was born. She sent the baby to be nursed among Banu Sa'd by Halima Al-Sa'deya. When he was six she took him to visit her relatives in Yathrib. On the way back to Makkah, with Umm Ayman, she fell ill and died at al-Abwa', where she was buried.\nAbu Huraira reported that the Prophet ﷺ visited his mother's grave and wept. He said: \"I sought permission from my Lord to beg forgiveness for her but it was not granted to me, and I sought permission to visit her grave and it was granted to me so visit the graves, for that makes you mindful of death.\" (Sahih Muslim 976b)",
      "keyTakeaway": "Aminah bint Wahb: Mother of the Prophet ﷺ; died at al-Abwa' when he was six.",
