      "title": "Umayma bint Abd al-Muttalib",
      "intro": "Known for: Paternal aunt of the Prophet ﷺ; mother of Zaynab bint Jahsh.",
      "explanationContent": "Known for: Paternal aunt of the Prophet ﷺ; mother of Zaynab bint Jahsh. Full name: Umayma bint Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim. Tribe: Quraysh, clan of Banu Hashim. Father: Abdul Muttalib. Born in Makkah.\nA full sister of the Prophet's ﷺ father Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib; their mother was Fatimah bint Amr of Banu Makhzum. She married Jahsh ibn Riyab of Asad ibn Khuzayma, and they had six children: Abd Allah, Ubayd Allah, Zaynab (later a wife of the Prophet ﷺ), Abu Ahmad, Habiba (Umm Habib) and Hamna. It is not recorded that she became a Muslim, and she did not go with her children on the Hijra. She was still alive in 628, when the Prophet ﷺ gave her a yearly share of the dates of Khaybar.",
      "keyTakeaway": "Umayma bint Abd al-Muttalib: Paternal aunt of the Prophet ﷺ; mother of Zaynab bint Jahsh.",
